          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11. A student said, “The Earth moves around the Sun”. In this context, discuss whether an object kept on the Earth can be considered to be at rest."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.226,
            0.145,
            0.89,
            0.197
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "12. The velocity-time graph from 0 s to 120 s for a cyclist is shown in Fig. 4.30. Shade the areas (in different colours) representing the displacement of the cyclist"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.196,
            0.712,
            0.215
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) while cyclist is moving with constant velocity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.264,
            0.214,
            0.672,
            0.231
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) when the velocity of cyclist is decreasing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.264,
            0.23,
            0.889,
            0.263
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Also, calculate the displacement and average acceleration in the 120 s time interval."
