            0.555
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13. A girl is preparing for her first marathon by running on a straight road. She uses a smartwatch to calculate her running speed at different intervals. The graph (Fig. 4.31) depicts her velocity versus time. Estimate the distance she ran based on the graph."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.227,
            0.556,
            0.89,
            0.641
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "14. On entering a state highway, a car continues to move with a constant velocity of 6 m "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbb { S } ^ { - 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for 2 minutes and then accelerates with a constant acceleration 1 m "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "S ^ { - 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for 6 seconds. Find the displacement of the car on the state highway in the 2 min 6 s time interval by drawing a velocity-time graph for its motion."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.225,
            0.643,
            0.89,
            0.762
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "15. Two cars A and B start moving with a constant acceleration from rest, in a straight line. Car A attains a velocity of 5 m "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbb { S } ^ { - 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in 5 s. Car B attains a velocity of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3    m     s ^{-1}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in 10 s. Plot the velocity-time graphs for both the cars in the same graph. Using the graph, calculate the displacement in the two time intervals mentioned (Hint: Calculate the acceleration in both cases. Then calculate their velocities at five instants of time to plot the graph)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.225,
            0.764,
            0.888,
            0.814
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "16. Rohan studies science from 6 PM to 7:30 PM at home. Consider the tip of the minute’s hand of the wall clock. During the given time interval, what is its: 1111111"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.819,
            0.471,
            0.837
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) distance travelled,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.263,
            0.837,
            0.432,
            0.853
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) displacement,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.259,
            0.854,
            0.405,
            0.87
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) speed, and"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.26,
            0.871,
            0.382,
            0.888
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) velocity."
